## 🧮 Part 1: Quaternion Mathematics

### 1.1 Basic Quaternion Operations

```python
# Create quaternions using different methods
print("=" * 60)
print("1.1 Quaternion Creation")
print("=" * 60)

# Method 1: Direct components
q1 = Quaternion(0.7071, 0.0, 0.0, 0.7071)
print(f"q1 (direct): {q1}")

# Method 2: From axis-angle
axis = np.array([0, 0, 1])  # Z-axis
angle = np.pi / 2  # 90 degrees
q2 = Quaternion.from_axis_angle(axis, angle)
print(f"q2 (axis-angle): {q2}")

# Method 3: From Euler angles (ZYX convention)
roll, pitch, yaw = np.pi/4, np.pi/6, np.pi/3
q3 = Quaternion.from_euler_angles(roll, pitch, yaw)
print(f"q3 (Euler): {q3}")

# Verify they're unit quaternions
print(f"\nNorms: q1={q1.norm:.6f}, q2={q2.norm:.6f}, q3={q3.norm:.6f}")
```

### 1.2 Quaternion Arithmetic

```python
print("\n" + "=" * 60)
print("1.2 Quaternion Arithmetic")
print("=" * 60)

# Addition
q_sum = q1 + q2
print(f"q1 + q2 = {q_sum}")

# Multiplication (Hamilton product)
q_prod = q1 * q2
print(f"q1 * q2 = {q_prod}")

# Conjugate
print(f"q1* = {q1.conjugate}")

# Inverse
print(f"q1⁻¹ = {q1.inverse}")

# Unit quaternion
print(f"q1̂ = {q1.unit}")
```

